Spec: Windows public connection execution

Purpose:
  Compose exact local visitor access, server leases, protected one-use data pipes and observed business accounting.

Owns:
  ./FormalConnections.cs
  ./IFormalConnections.cs

References:
  ./ConnectionJournal.sdd
  ./ConnectionMeter.sdd
  ./ConnectionPlanner.sdd
  ./SecureConnections.sdd

Must:
  When an explicit scoped provider is configured, try a short owner-known LAN candidate then XTCP, with terminal authentication failures never falling back; use dynamic relay only when policy permits.
  Offer experimental connection.api only with explicitly configured server authority and an owner-started secure host; never downgrade to preview authentication.
  Capture original monotonic admission before storage and use requested approved policy with authenticated direct endpoints and exact owned relay routes.
  Keep at most 32 live formal entries and 16 per caller, share the durable combined limits, and return retained operations before resource admission without redial.
  Create data pipe names only from retained streamRef, pin actual pipe clients to their OS caller and consume attachment once after a bounded header; keep the total attach budget ten seconds.
  Count successful business writes per selected path, preserve FIN/backpressure, mark complete only after both drains and persist cumulative snapshots on an owned periodic monitor.
  Close raw sockets, pipes and late transports on cancellation, grant loss, host stop or network-generation invalidation; closing one flow cannot close unrelated flows.
  Expose only DTOs and reference values, never candidates, process paths, device keys or caller-submitted dial targets.
  Keep physical network observation separate from scoped runtime acquisition; expose no unverified physical network claims.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Verify public SDK delivery, retained operations, one-use caller-bound pipes, exact counters and independent cancellation through actual authenticated direct/relay transports.
